  "country_briefings": {
    "GBR": "A historical global fleet at a turning point. Treaty parity with America means scrapping battleships while guarding distant sea lanes.",
    "USA": "A historical battle fleet with vast industrial backing. Washington halts the building race; carrier conversions and two-ocean defense shape the next navy.",
    "JPN": "A historical Pacific fleet under the three-fifths limit. Canceled battleships make carrier conversions, training and superior individual ships the path forward.",
    "FRA": "A historical navy rebuilding after the Great War. Treaty parity with Italy leaves Atlantic commitments competing with Mediterranean security.",
    "ITA": "A historical fleet concentrated in the Mediterranean. Parity with France offers status, but aging battleships and limited funds demand careful modernization.",
    "DEU": "The historical Reichsmarine begins under Versailles, outside Washington. Old battleships, a small personnel ceiling and a submarine ban constrain every ambition.",
    "SOV": "Civil war has left the historical fleet scattered and worn. Outside Washington, Soviet Russia must restore crews and industry before building anew."
  }
